    "['locator [parameter1] ipv6-prefix [parameter2] [parameter3] static [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing prefix-sid-map ipv6 2001:db8:15::/64 range 32 static', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco command for the HUAWEI segment routing IPv6 locator configuration:\\n\\n##\\nsegment-routing prefix-sid-map ipv6 2001:db8:15::/64 range 32 static\\n##\\n\\nThis Cisco command:\\n1. Creates an IPv6 prefix SID mapping for the specified prefix (2001:db8:15::/64)\\n2. Specifies a static range of 32 SIDs\\n3. Matches the functionality of the HUAWEI locator configuration which defines a prefix and static SID allocation space\\n\\nNote that Cisco\\'s implementation uses different terminology (\"prefix-sid-map\" instead of \"locator\") but achieves the same fundamental purpose of mapping IPv6 prefixes to Segment Routing identifiers.', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing prefix-sid-map ipv6 2001:db8:15::/64 range 32 static'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 1', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing prefix-sid-map ipv6 2001:db8:15::/64 range 32 static'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `opcode ::1 end` command assigns a static SID (Segment Identifier) with value ::1 and marks it as an \"end\" SID (which represents the router itself in SRv6).\\n- The Cisco equivalent uses `prefix-sid index` under the SRv6 locator configuration to achieve the same functionality.\\n- The index value \"1\" corresponds to the ::1 SID in the Huawei configuration (assuming the locator prefix is 2001:db8:15::, then ::1 would be 2001:db8:15::1).', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 1'}]]": 1,
    "['opcode [parameter1] end-dt4 vpn-instance [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 100 vpn-private-ipv4', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing prefix-sid-map ipv6 2001:db8:15::/64 range 32 static'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nsegment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 100 vpn-private-ipv4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `opcode ::100 end-dt4 vpn-instance vpna` command creates a SID for IPv4 VPN End.DT4 functionality (Endpoint with decapsulation and IPv4 table lookup) in the SRv6 locator.\\n- The Cisco equivalent uses `prefix-sid index` to assign the SID value (100 in this case) with `vpn-private-ipv4` specifying the End.DT4 behavior for VPN IPv4 traffic.\\n- The locator name (`as1`) is maintained between both configurations.\\n- Note that Cisco's implementation might require additional context or configuration for the VPN instance mapping.\", 'trans_template': 'segment-routing ipv6 locator as1 prefix-sid index 100 vpn-private-ipv4'}]]": 1,
